{title: 530 - It Is Well With My Soul}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #530 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 530}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]When peace like a river, [G7/F]attendeth my way,
[G7]When sorrows [C]like sea [Am]billows [Bdim]roll
[F/C]Whatever [G/D]my lot, [Dm]thou [G]hast [G7]taught me [C]to say
[Em]It is [F]well, it is [Em]well, [Dm]with my soul.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Dm]It [G]is well [G7/F]with [C/E]my soul,
[F]it is well, [C/G]it is [G]well with my soul.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]My sin--oh, the joy [G7/F]of [Em]this [G7/D]glorious thought--
[G7]My sin, [C]not in part but [Am]the whole,
[F/C]is nailed [Am/C]to [G/D]the cross, [Dm]and [G]I [G7]bear it [C]no more,
[Em]praise the [F]Lord, praise the [Em]Lord, [Dm]O my soul!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]And, Lord, haste the day when [G7/F]my [Em]faith [G7/D]shall be sight,
[G7]the clouds [C]be rolled back [Am]as a [Bdim]scroll;
[F/C]the trump [Am/C]shall [G/D]resound, [Dm]and [G]the [G7]Lord shall [C]descend,
[Em]even [F]so, it is [Em]well [Dm]with my soul.
{end_of_verse}
